---
import CourseLayout from "../layouts/CourseLayout.astro";
---

<CourseLayout title="Accessibility Statement">
  <div class="accessibility-page">
    <h1>Accessibility Statement</h1>

    <p>We are committed to making this C# learning platform accessible to all students and users, including those with disabilities.</p>

    <h2>Accessibility Standards</h2>

    <p>This site is designed to conform to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Section 508 accessibility guidelines</strong></li>
    </ul>

    <p>Accessibility features implemented include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Full <strong>keyboard navigation support</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Skip-to-content navigation</strong></li>
      <li>Logical <strong>heading structure and landmarks</strong></li>
      <li><strong>ARIA labeling</strong> for interactive controls</li>
      <li><strong>Accessible form validation and error messaging</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Screen reader announcements for dynamic content</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Color contrast compliant with WCAG AA</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Alternative text for images and diagrams</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Text descriptions for complex instructional diagrams</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Reduced motion support</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Responsive layout that works at 200% zoom</strong></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Screen Reader Support</h2>

    <p>This platform has been tested with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>NVDA (Windows)</li>
      <li>VoiceOver (macOS)</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Major learning components tested include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>AI Tutor panel</li>
      <li>Interactive quizzes</li>
      <li>Knowledge checks</li>
      <li>Instructor dashboards</li>
      <li>Code editors and lab runners</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Keyboard Navigation</h2>

    <p>All functionality on this site can be used with a keyboard.</p>
    <p>Key interactions include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Tab / Shift+Tab</strong> to move between controls</li>
      <li><strong>Enter / Space</strong> to activate buttons</li>
      <li><strong>Escape</strong> to close dialogs or panels</li>
      <li><strong>Arrow keys</strong> to navigate menus where appropriate</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Known Exceptions</h2>

    <p>Some code blocks may allow <strong>horizontal scrolling</strong> due to the nature of programming examples. This behavior is intentional to preserve code formatting.</p>

    <h2>Reporting Accessibility Issues</h2>

    <p>If you encounter an accessibility barrier while using this site, please report it.</p>
    <p>Include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The page URL</li>
      <li>The issue encountered</li>
      <li>Your assistive technology (if applicable)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Accessibility issues will be reviewed and addressed as quickly as possible.</p>

    <h2>Continuous Improvement</h2>

    <p>Accessibility is an ongoing effort. This site is periodically tested using:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Automated accessibility tools</li>
      <li>Keyboard navigation testing</li>
      <li>Screen reader testing</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We are committed to improving accessibility for all learners.</p>
  </div>
</CourseLayout>

<style>
  .accessibility-page {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .accessibility-page h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .accessibility-page h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .accessibility-page p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .accessibility-page ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .accessibility-page li {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
</style>
